        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
                "word": "chartisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "df1033a8-0574-4093-89de-cac4c49e6ee9",
                        "entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "chartismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c7e56da7-d03e-3895-84a0-af1fa2c192b0",
                        "entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mouvement social ouvrier en Angleterre entre 1838 et 1848."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2edd3e1c-650f-471c-8012-c0c6421f135c",
                                "sense_id": "c7e56da7-d03e-3895-84a0-af1fa2c192b0",
                                "text": "Le chartisme, cette plaie terrible, était constitué, et, jusque aux portes de Londres la population inquiète des tisserands de soie de Spitael-Fields, poussait, dans d’innombrables meetings, des cris de haine contre la métropole."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d22efd23-787c-3728-858f-efa771941602",
                        "entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Limitation des pouvoirs d’un peuple souverain par une série de chartes et de traités."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e37ef48-6873-4d02-9be3-98364408ecdb",
                                "sense_id": "d22efd23-787c-3728-858f-efa771941602",
                                "text": "Maxime Tandonnet décrit ce que Mathieu Bock-Coté appelle le chartisme : à coups de chartes et de traités, on limite de plus en plus les pouvoirs du peuple souverain."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0439a86a-22ca-38ec-9d09-16606022c496",
                        "entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Technique d’analyse boursière reposant sur les graphiques des cours de bourse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "daf0e0b6-350a-4b27-b782-9ddf3b5436f8",
                                "sense_id": "0439a86a-22ca-38ec-9d09-16606022c496",
                                "text": "Le chartisme est une méthode d'analyse basée sur la reconnaissance de “figures types” (Triangle, Biseau, ETE, Flag, etc…) et permettant d'appréhender l’évolution du marché boursier."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5b481642-03cd-4fdd-8c1a-5af61f2d76f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mouvement social ouvrier en Angleterre",
                        "target_lang_word": "Chartism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Chartism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffb123c7-41de-3b85-83b3-246dd72537ed",
                                        "entry_id": "c2596f0e-7ddc-3d58-b1e0-f84a90ca74db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A working-class movement for political and social reform in the United Kingdom during the mid-19th century."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ab2b0ca-fc9a-4c8a-af23-454e59141838",
                                                "sense_id": "ffb123c7-41de-3b85-83b3-246dd72537ed",
                                                "text": "An insincere world; a godless untruth of a world! It is out of this, as I consider, that the whole tribe of social pestilences, French Revolutions, Chartisms, and what not, have derived their being,—their chief necessity to be."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4164b73b-6e31-479c-85f6-f7ab4e6bc2e5",
                                                "sense_id": "ffb123c7-41de-3b85-83b3-246dd72537ed",
                                                "text": "[…] when she married the young clergyman, and went to settle in that smoky hole Turley; a very nest of Chartism and Atheism, in a part of the country which all the decent families had had to leave for years."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a23abc0-042a-4274-804b-a224495efc69",
                                                "sense_id": "ffb123c7-41de-3b85-83b3-246dd72537ed",
                                                "text": "Chartism therefore, though a genuine popular movement, was incomplete in its aims and knowledge; the time was not yet come and it could not triumph openly; but it would be a mistake to say that it failed utterly: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c0f3ec3-2054-49cd-939c-2772115b684c",
                                                "sense_id": "ffb123c7-41de-3b85-83b3-246dd72537ed",
                                                "text": "The dangers of this revolutionary ferment were grave; even in England Chartism was rampant—a sinister movement, which might at any moment upset the Constitution and abolish the Monarchy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfcf59f3-dbb3-4c04-9316-ee2ba8018a6c",
                                                "sense_id": "ffb123c7-41de-3b85-83b3-246dd72537ed",
                                                "text": "When Owenism and Chartism had burned themselves out, England had become poorer by that substance out of which the Anglo-Saxon ideal of a free society could have been built up for centuries to come."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7fc9eea8-0a82-4133-a0ff-d0a05e117b47",
                        "source_entry_id": "22107bff-eb00-3aab-a96b-759fec203565",
